<title>PORTUGAL: Portuguese seven-month car sales fall 3.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Portuguese seven-month car sales fall 3.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Portuguese Auto Dealers Association (ACAP) announced the following new car sales:</p>
<p>    July 1997	 22,229 vs  23,346 (down 4.8 pct)</p>
<p>Jan/July 1997	134,356 vs 139,612 (down 3.8 pct)</p>
<p>First seven months by manufacturers' markets share (percentage in brackets). Comparative figures refer to same period 1996:</p>
<p> Opel	   18,792 (13.99) vs 20,514 (14.69)</p>
<p> Fiat	   16,935 (12.60) vs 20,955 (15.01)</p>
<p> Renault	16,762 (12.48) vs 18,255 (13.08)</p>
<p> Ford	   14,111 (10.50) vs 13,961 (10.00)</p>
<p> Volkswagen   12,529 (9.33)  vs 11,607  (8.31)</p>
<p> Citroen	9,603  (7.15)  vs  7,856  (5.63)</p>
<p> Peugeot	8,541  (6.36)  vs  9,180  (6.58)</p>
<p> Honda	  4,739  (3.53)  vs  4,788  (3.43)</p>
<p> Seat	   4,307  (3.21)  vs  4,635  (3.32)</p>
<p> Rover	  3,522  (2.62)  vs  5,212  (3.73)</p>
<p>-- Lisboa Editorial.351.1.31131247</p>
</text>
